# Agents and tools

## Tools

```ts
// ✅ build per request with RequestContext
build(ctx: RequestContext) {
  return tool({
    description: '...',
    inputSchema: z.object({ orderId: z.string() }),
    execute: ({ orderId }) => this.orders.findForUser(ctx.userId, orderId),
  });
}
```

- Register in `ToolsModule`; inject only into agents that should have the tool.
- Add `*.tool.spec.ts` with a fixed `RequestContext`.
- Do not put controllers or agent instructions in tool files.

## Agents

- `create(ctx)` returns `new ToolLoopAgent({ ... })` — instructions, tools map, step limit / `stopWhen`.
- Unique `readonly id` for `agentId` on `POST /chat`.
- Export from `AgentsModule`; `register` in `AgentRegistry` constructor.
- No Express types, no persistence, no provider API keys in agent files.

Copy `order-lookup.tool.ts` / `assistant.agent.ts` rather than inventing new shapes.
